internal/ssprove/wots/bound/chain_tcr.v
internal/ssprove/wots/bound/chain_pre.v
internal/ssprove/wots/bound/prf.v
internal/ssprove/wots/theorem.v
# --- ssprove: the model at the functions of spec.v ---
# shape.v relates the loops of spec.v to closed forms, instance.v builds
# the parameter record from spec.v and proves the model's scheme equal to
# the specification's, and security.v states the two SSProve conjuncts.
internal/ssprove/shape.v
internal/ssprove/instance.v
internal/ssprove/security.v

# --- the honesty gate ---
# audit/probe.v and audit/statement.v are intentionally NOT listed here,
# i.e. not part of the default build: probe.v is an axiom-fetch-heavy
# `Print Assumptions` tail over the whole cone, and statement.v exists to
# be type-checked against the built theorem, which only makes sense once
# that theorem is built. `make audit` / audit/check.sh compiles each
# standalone with coqc (gates 4 and 5), so the audit is unaffected; both
# resolve under the same `-Q . Shrincs` root as everything else (and so
# editor tooling reading this file resolves them too).

# Public statements compose completed results over the canonical specification.
theorem.v
